IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Arizona Revised Statutes, Title 43 (Taxation of Income) -- the income tax of a full-year resident individual.
--
-- Edition: the Legislature's online A.R.S. (unofficial; "updated to include the revised sections from the 57th
-- Legislature, 2nd Regular Session"), deposited at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/az-ars-43-ch1-general-provisions-sel-2026.txt   (ss 43-102, 43-104, 43-105; 2026-10-19)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/az-ars-43-ch10-individuals-sel-2026.txt         (ss 43-1001 to 43-1073.01 selected; 2026-10-19)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/az-ars-43-ss243-301-501-2026-10-24.txt          (ss 43-243, 43-301, 43-501; 2026-10-24)
--
-- In: s 43-104(19) (resident); s 43-301(A), (E) (who must file); s 43-501 (when payable); s 43-1001 (Arizona gross income is
-- federal AGI; Arizona AGI; taxable income); s 43-1021 (additions, one total); s 43-1022(1), (2), (10), (26) (exemptions,
-- public pensions to $2,500, Social Security, uniformed services retired pay; the rest as one total); s 43-1023 (exemptions:
-- blind, 65 or older, dependants in care, stillbirth, a parent in the home); s 43-1041(A), (C), (D), (F), (H), (I)(2)
-- (standard deduction, the election, and the charitable increase from 2026); s 43-1011(A)(7)-(9) with s 43-243 (which
-- rate table applies); s 43-1072.01 (the increased excise tax credit); s 43-1073 (family income tax credit);
-- s 43-1073.01 (dependent tax credit).
--
-- Annual figures: the standard deduction is adjusted for inflation each year from 2020 "in the same manner" as the federal
-- one (s 43-1041(H)); the department's adjusted figures are not deposited. The figures in s 43-1041(A) are used for the
-- 2025 taxable year only; for other years the person states the department's figure (NOTES.md finding 2). The s 43-1011
-- paragraph 7 and 8 brackets are inflation-indexed (subsection E) and not deposited, so only paragraph 9 (flat 2.5%) is
-- computed. Whether and when the s 43-243 notices were received is a fact the person (or a later deposit) supplies.
--
-- Out: nonresidents and part-year residents (`not covered`); itemised deductions item by item (s 43-1042: one total); the
-- other credits (s 43-1071 other-state tax, s 43-1072 property tax credit, and the credits not deposited); s 43-1011(A)(1)
-- -(6) (years before 2022) and s 43-1013 (surcharge); the small business income tax (s 43-1022(28), ch. 17).
--
-- Federal links (not imported: the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across folders): federal adjusted gross income, the amount of
-- Social Security included under IRC s 86, and "dependent" (IRC s 152) come from subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986,
-- as the Code stood on the s 43-105 conformity date.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, from the seat of the individual taxpayer. Expected values in the case file are hand-written. No
-- pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT TAX ADVICE.

§ `A.R.S. Title 43 -- the individual income tax`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    `the tax of a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded`
    -- s 43-1011(A)(1)-(6)
    `this encoding computes the tax for taxable years from 2022 only`
    -- s 43-1011(A)(7), (8) with (E): brackets adjusted each year by the department, not deposited
    `the s 43-1011 paragraph 7 or 8 brackets apply, and their inflation-adjusted amounts are not deposited`
    -- s 43-1041(H)
    `the department's inflation-adjusted standard deduction for this year was not supplied`
    -- s 43-1041(I)(1): a percentage the department adjusts, not deposited
    `the 2025 charitable increase to the standard deduction uses a percentage the department adjusts, not deposited`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Filing status`

-- s 43-1001(5), (6), (9); s 43-1002: "married person", "single person", "head of household" (IRC s 2(b), (c), including a
-- surviving spouse under s 2(a)), asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `married filing separately`
    `head of household`
    `married filing jointly`

§§ `s 43-104(19) -- resident`

-- (a) "Every individual who is in this state for other than a temporary or transitory purpose"; (b) every individual
-- domiciled here and outside the state for a temporary or transitory purpose; (c) more than nine months in the aggregate
-- "shall be presumed to be a resident", which "may be overcome by competent evidence that the individual is in this state
-- for a temporary or transitory purpose".
GIVEN `in Arizona for other than a temporary or transitory purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `domiciled in Arizona and away only temporarily`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `months in Arizona in the taxable year`                     IS A NUMBER
      `the presumption is overcome`                               IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a resident` IF
        `in Arizona for other than a temporary or transitory purpose`
    OR  `domiciled in Arizona and away only temporarily`
    OR  (`months in Arizona in the taxable year` GREATER THAN 9 AND (NOT (`the presumption is overcome`)))

§§ `s 43-1041 -- the optional standard deduction`

-- (A), "subject to subsection H": $15,750 single or married filing separately; $23,625 head of household; $31,500 joint.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the standard deduction in subsection A` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `single`                    THEN 15750
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 15750
    WHEN `head of household`         THEN 23625
    WHEN `married filing jointly`    THEN 31500

-- (H): adjusted for inflation for each taxable year from 2020. The (A) figures are read as the 2025 figures (finding 2);
-- for any other year the department's figure must be supplied (0 if not known).
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER, `status` IS A `Filing status`, `the department's figure for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the standard deduction for the year` MEANS
    IF `the department's figure for the year` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `answered` `the department's figure for the year`
    ELSE IF `tax year` EQUALS 2025
         THEN `answered` (`the standard deduction in subsection A` `status`)
         ELSE `not covered` `the department's inflation-adjusted standard deduction for this year was not supplied`

-- (I)(2): from 2026 the standard deduction is increased by the charitable contributions (IRC s 170(c)), at most $1,000 for
-- "a single person or a married person filing separately" and $2,000 for "a married couple filing a joint return". A head
-- of household is "a single person who is a head of a household" (s 43-1041(A)(2)) and takes the $1,000 cap (finding 3).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `charitable contributions` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the charitable increase from 2026` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly`
    THEN min 2000 `charitable contributions`
    ELSE min 1000 `charitable contributions`

§§ `s 43-1023 -- exemptions`

DECLARE `Exemption facts` HAS
    -- (A): $1,500 for a taxpayer who is blind, and for a blind spouse with no Arizona AGI on the taxpayer's separate return
    `blind persons qualifying`                               IS A NUMBER
    -- (E): $2,100 for a taxpayer 65 or older not claimed as another's dependent, and for such a spouse on a joint return
    `persons 65 or older qualifying`                         IS A NUMBER
    -- (B)(1): $2,300 for each person 65 or older for whose institutional or medical care the taxpayer pays as (B) says
    `persons 65 or older whose care I pay for`               IS A NUMBER
    -- (B)(2): $2,300 for each stillbirth in the year
    `stillbirths in the year`                                IS A NUMBER
    -- (C): $10,000 for each parent or ancestor 65 or older needing help with daily living, living in the home all year,
    -- more than half of whose support the taxpayer pays (in lieu of (B) for the same person)
    `parents 65 or older living with me whom I support`      IS A NUMBER

GIVEN e IS AN `Exemption facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 43-1023 exemptions` MEANS
        (1500  TIMES e's `blind persons qualifying`)
    PLUS (2100 TIMES e's `persons 65 or older qualifying`)
    PLUS (2300 TIMES e's `persons 65 or older whose care I pay for`)
    PLUS (2300 TIMES e's `stillbirths in the year`)
    PLUS (10000 TIMES e's `parents 65 or older living with me whom I support`)

§§ `s 43-1022 -- subtractions; s 43-1001 -- Arizona adjusted gross income and taxable income`

DECLARE `Return` HAS
    `tax year`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `full-year resident`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `status`                                            IS A `Filing status`
    `federal adjusted gross income`                     IS A NUMBER
    `additions`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `exemption facts`                                   IS AN `Exemption facts`
    -- s 43-1022(2): federal, state and local public pensions, "not more than $2,500"; one figure per return (finding 4)
    `public pensions received`                          IS A NUMBER
    -- s 43-1022(10): "The amount included in federal adjusted gross income pursuant to section 86"
    `Social Security included in federal AGI`           IS A NUMBER
    -- s 43-1022(26)(c): uniformed services retired or retainer pay, "the full amount received" from 2021
    `uniformed services retired pay`                    IS A NUMBER
    `other subtractions`                                IS A NUMBER
    `elects the standard deduction`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemized deductions`                               IS A NUMBER
    `charitable contributions`                          IS A NUMBER
    `the department's standard deduction for the year`  IS A NUMBER
    -- s 43-243: the year each notice was received by the department (0 if not received)
    `year of the s 43-243(B)(2) notice`                 IS A NUMBER
    `year of the s 43-243(A) or (B)(1) notice`          IS A NUMBER
    `dependents under 17`                               IS A NUMBER
    `dependents 17 or older`                            IS A NUMBER
    -- s 43-1072.01
    `claimed as a dependent by another taxpayer`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `sentenced to custody for 60 days or more`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `residents in the household for the excise credit`  IS A NUMBER

GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the subtractions` MEANS
        `the s 43-1023 exemptions` (r's `exemption facts`)
    PLUS min 2500 (r's `public pensions received`)
    PLUS r's `Social Security included in federal AGI`
    PLUS r's `uniformed services retired pay`
    PLUS r's `other subtractions`

-- s 43-1001(1), (2): Arizona gross income is federal AGI; Arizona AGI is that "subject to modifications specified in
-- sections 43-1021 and 43-1022".
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Arizona adjusted gross income` MEANS
    r's `federal adjusted gross income` PLUS r's `additions` MINUS `the subtractions` r

-- s 43-1001(11): "Arizona adjusted gross income less the deductions allowed in article 4".
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the deduction` MEANS
    IF NOT (r's `elects the standard deduction`)
    THEN `answered` (r's `itemized deductions`)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the standard deduction for the year` (r's `tax year`) (r's `status`) (r's `the department's standard deduction for the year`)
         WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
         WHEN `answered` `base` THEN
             IF r's `tax year` AT LEAST 2026
             THEN `answered` (`base` PLUS `the charitable increase from 2026` (r's `status`) (r's `charitable contributions`))
             ELSE IF r's `charitable contributions` GREATER THAN 0
                  THEN `not covered` `the 2025 charitable increase to the standard deduction uses a percentage the department adjusts, not deposited`
                  ELSE `answered` `base`

§§ `s 43-1011 with s 43-243 -- the rate`

-- s 43-243(D): on the (B)(2) notice "the department shall use the tax rates provided in section 43-1011, subsection A,
-- paragraph 9 for taxable years beginning from and after December 31 of the year in which the notice ... is received".
-- (C): the (A) or (B)(1) notice switches to paragraph 8 the same way, until the (B)(2) notice. Paragraph 7 otherwise.
-- Paragraph 9: "the tax is 2.5% of taxable income".
GIVEN r IS A `Return`, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the tax on taxable income` MEANS
    IF r's `year of the s 43-243(B)(2) notice` GREATER THAN 0 AND r's `tax year` GREATER THAN r's `year of the s 43-243(B)(2) notice`
    THEN `answered` (2.5% TIMES `taxable income`)
    ELSE `not covered` `the s 43-1011 paragraph 7 or 8 brackets apply, and their inflation-adjusted amounts are not deposited`

§§ `Credits`

-- s 43-1073.01(B), (C): $125 for each dependent under 17 and $25 for each dependent 17 or older; at or above $200,000 of
-- federal AGI ($400,000 joint), each "minus five percent for each $1,000, or fraction thereof, by which the taxpayer's
-- federal adjusted gross income exceeds the applicable threshold" (read as 5% of the amount: finding 5). Dependents for
-- whom a s 43-1023(B) or (C) exemption is claimed are excluded by the person (s 43-1023(D)).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent credit factor` MEANS
    IF `federal adjusted gross income` LESS THAN `the dependent credit threshold` `status`
    THEN 1
    ELSE max 0 (1 MINUS (5% TIMES `the thousands over` (`federal adjusted gross income` MINUS `the dependent credit threshold` `status`)))

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent credit threshold` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly`
    THEN 400000
    ELSE 200000

-- "for each $1,000, or fraction thereof"
GIVEN `excess` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the thousands over` MEANS
    IF FLOOR (`excess` DIVIDED BY 1000) EQUALS (`excess` DIVIDED BY 1000)
    THEN `excess` DIVIDED BY 1000
    ELSE FLOOR (`excess` DIVIDED BY 1000) PLUS 1

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER, `under 17` IS A NUMBER, `17 or older` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the dependent tax credit` MEANS
    ((125 TIMES `under 17`) PLUS (25 TIMES `17 or older`)) TIMES `the dependent credit factor` `status` `federal adjusted gross income`

-- s 43-1073(A): the income limits by status and number of dependents, tested against Arizona AGI "plus the amount
-- subtracted for exemptions under section 43-1023".
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `dependents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family credit income limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `married filing jointly` THEN
        BRANCH IF `dependents` AT MOST 1 THEN 20000
               IF `dependents` EQUALS 2 THEN 23600
               IF `dependents` EQUALS 3 THEN 27300
               OTHERWISE 31000
    WHEN `head of household` THEN
        BRANCH IF `dependents` AT MOST 1 THEN 20000
               IF `dependents` EQUALS 2 THEN 20135
               IF `dependents` EQUALS 3 THEN 23800
               IF `dependents` EQUALS 4 THEN 25200
               OTHERWISE 26575
    WHEN `single` THEN 10000
    WHEN `married filing separately` THEN 10000

-- s 43-1073(B): $40 for each resident who is the taxpayer, a spouse who does not file a return, or a dependent; at most
-- $240 (joint or head of household) or $120 (single or separate), and at most the tax due.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `Arizona AGI plus exemptions` IS A NUMBER, `dependents` IS A NUMBER, `tax due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family income tax credit` MEANS
    IF `Arizona AGI plus exemptions` GREATER THAN `the family credit income limit` `status` `dependents`
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `tax due` (min (`the family credit cap` `status`) (40 TIMES (`the persons for the family credit` `status` `dependents`)))

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the family credit cap` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `status` EQUALS `head of household`
    THEN 240
    ELSE 120

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `dependents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the persons for the family credit` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly`
    THEN 2 PLUS `dependents`
    ELSE 1 PLUS `dependents`

-- s 43-1072.01(A), (C), (F): federal AGI of $25,000 or less (a married couple or head of household) or $12,500 or less
-- (single or married filing separately); not claimed as a dependent; not sentenced to custody for 60 days of the year;
-- $25 for each resident for whom an exemption is allowed, at most $100. (D): refundable.
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER, `claimed as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN, `in custody 60 days` IS A BOOLEAN, `residents` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the increased excise tax credit` MEANS
    IF `claimed as a dependent` OR `in custody 60 days` OR `federal adjusted gross income` GREATER THAN `the excise credit income limit` `status`
    THEN 0
    ELSE min 100 (25 TIMES `residents`)

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excise credit income limit` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing jointly` OR `status` EQUALS `head of household`
    THEN 25000
    ELSE 12500

§§ `The tax`

-- Tax on taxable income, less the dependent and family credits (nonrefundable: finding 6), less the refundable excise tax
-- credit. A negative answer is a refund.
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the tax after credits` MEANS
    IF NOT (r's `full-year resident`)
    THEN `not covered` `the tax of a nonresident or part-year resident is not encoded`
    ELSE IF r's `tax year` LESS THAN 2022
         THEN `not covered` `this encoding computes the tax for taxable years from 2022 only`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the deduction` r
              WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
              WHEN `answered` `deduction` THEN
                  CONSIDER `the tax on taxable income` r (max 0 (`the Arizona adjusted gross income` r MINUS `deduction`))
                  WHEN `not covered` `why` THEN `not covered` `why`
                  WHEN `answered` `tax` THEN `answered` (`the net tax` r `tax`)

GIVEN r IS A `Return`, `tax` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net tax` MEANS
    (max 0 ((`tax` MINUS `dependent credit`) MINUS `family credit`)) MINUS `excise credit`
    WHERE
        `dependent credit` MEANS `the dependent tax credit` (r's `status`) (r's `federal adjusted gross income`) (r's `dependents under 17`) (r's `dependents 17 or older`)
        `family credit` MEANS `the family income tax credit` (r's `status`) (`the Arizona adjusted gross income` r PLUS `the s 43-1023 exemptions` (r's `exemption facts`)) (r's `dependents under 17` PLUS r's `dependents 17 or older`) `tax`
        `excise credit` MEANS `the increased excise tax credit` (r's `status`) (r's `federal adjusted gross income`) (r's `claimed as a dependent by another taxpayer`) (r's `sentenced to custody for 60 days or more`) (r's `residents in the household for the excise credit`)

§§ `s 43-301 -- who must file`

-- (A): a full-year or part-year resident "shall file a return ... if ... the individual's gross income was greater than the
-- amount of the standard deduction allowed under ... 43-1041, subsection A as adjusted for inflation". (E): gross income is
-- IRC gross income less income included but excluded from taxation under Title 43.
GIVEN `gross income` IS A NUMBER, `standard deduction for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `required to file` IF
    `gross income` GREATER THAN `standard deduction for the year`

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF `the taxpayer`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file a return with the department`
    `pay the tax`
    `elect the standard deduction on the return`
    `change the election after filing`

-- s 43-301(A): "shall file a return with the department". The due date of the return is in a section not deposited
-- (finding 7), so no WITHIN.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to file` `who` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `file a return with the department`

-- s 43-501: "The tax imposed under this title shall be paid on the fifteenth day of April following the close of the
-- calendar year". Days count from the close of the year.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`, `days to 15 April` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to pay` `who` `days to 15 April` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `pay the tax`
    WITHIN `days to 15 April`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 43-501: tax not paid by 15 April"

-- s 43-1041(A), (C): "A taxpayer may elect to take a standard deduction", by claiming it on the return. (F): the election
-- may be changed after the return is filed, except as (G) says (a spouse's separate return not changed to match, or a
-- compromised liability).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`, `may change` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the standard deduction election` `who` `may change` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MAY   `elect the standard deduction on the return`
    HENCE
        IF `may change`
        THEN PARTY `who`
             MAY   `change the election after filing`
        ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the day tax is payable` MEANS Date 15 4 (`calendar year` PLUS 1)

-- s 43-1041(G): the election cannot be changed if the spouse filed a separate return and does not change to match (with
-- the consent to assessment), or if the liability has been compromised.
GIVEN `spouse filed a separate return` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse changes to match and both consent` IS A BOOLEAN, `liability compromised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may change the standard deduction election` IF
        (NOT (`liability compromised`))
    AND (    NOT (`spouse filed a separate return`)
         OR  `spouse changes to match and both consent`)

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the taxpayer`
-- The seat: the individual Arizona taxpayer. Each question is derived from the rules above.

§§ `Am I a resident? Must I file?`

@export Am I an Arizona resident for income tax (A.R.S. s 43-104(19))?
GIVEN `I am in Arizona for more than a temporary purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you in Arizona for other than a temporary or transitory purpose?
      `Arizona is my domicile and I am away only temporarily` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is Arizona your domicile, and are you outside the state only for a temporary or transitory purpose?
      `months I spent in Arizona` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many months of the taxable year did you spend in Arizona?
      `I can show my stay was temporary` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you spent more than nine months in Arizona: can you show by competent evidence that you were here only for a temporary or transitory purpose?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I an Arizona resident` MEANS
    `a resident` `I am in Arizona for more than a temporary purpose` `Arizona is my domicile and I am away only temporarily` `months I spent in Arizona` `I can show my stay was temporary`

@export Must I file an Arizona individual income tax return (A.R.S. s 43-301(A))?
GIVEN `my gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income for the year under the Internal Revenue Code, less income Arizona excludes from tax, in US dollars
      `the Arizona standard deduction for my status this year` IS A NUMBER @desc The Arizona standard deduction for your filing status for the year as adjusted for inflation (2025: $15,750 single or married filing separately, $23,625 head of household, $31,500 joint)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I file an Arizona return` MEANS
    `required to file` `my gross income` `the Arizona standard deduction for my status this year`

@export By what date must I pay my Arizona income tax for a calendar year (A.R.S. s 43-501)?
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the tax is for
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must I pay my Arizona tax` MEANS
    `the day tax is payable` `tax year`

§§ `Exemptions and credits`

@export How much are my Arizona exemptions for age, blindness, dependants in care, stillbirth and a parent at home (A.R.S. s 43-1023)?
GIVEN `blind people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (and your spouse on a joint return, or a blind spouse with no income on your separate return) are blind?
      `people 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (and your spouse on a joint return) were 65 or older by the end of the year and are not claimed as someone else's dependent?
      `older people whose care I pay for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many people 65 or older did you pay over a quarter of nursing or residential care costs (over $800), or over $800 of home health or medical care?
      `stillbirths` IS A NUMBER @desc How many stillbirths with a certificate occurred in your household this year?
      `parents at home I support` IS A NUMBER @desc How many parents or grandparents 65 or older, needing help with daily living, lived in your home all year with more than half their support paid by you?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my Arizona exemptions` MEANS
    `the s 43-1023 exemptions` (`Exemption facts` WITH
        `blind persons qualifying`                          IS `blind people`
        `persons 65 or older qualifying`                    IS `people 65 or older`
        `persons 65 or older whose care I pay for`          IS `older people whose care I pay for`
        `stillbirths in the year`                           IS `stillbirths`
        `parents 65 or older living with me whom I support` IS `parents at home I support`)

@export How much is my Arizona dependent tax credit (A.R.S. s 43-1073.01)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married filing separately, head of household or married filing jointly
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `dependents under 17` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents were under 17 at the end of the year (leave out anyone you claim an age-65 exemption for)?
      `dependents 17 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents were 17 or older at the end of the year (leave out anyone you claim an age-65 exemption for)?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my dependent tax credit` MEANS
    `the dependent tax credit` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `dependents under 17` `dependents 17 or older`

@export How much is my Arizona increased excise tax credit, which is paid even if I owe no tax (A.R.S. s 43-1072.01)?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married filing separately, head of household or married filing jointly
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `someone claims me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another taxpayer claim you as a dependent?
      `I was in custody 60 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to at least 60 days of the year in prison or jail?
      `residents in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Arizona residents in your household (you, your spouse, your dependents) have an exemption on your return?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my excise tax credit` MEANS
    `the increased excise tax credit` `my filing status` `my federal adjusted gross income` `someone claims me as a dependent` `I was in custody 60 days` `residents in my household`

§§ `How much do I owe?`

@export How much Arizona income tax do I owe as a full-year resident, after the dependent, family and excise credits (A.R.S. ss 43-1001 to 43-1073.01)? A negative amount is a refund.
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The taxable year, e.g. 2025
      `I was a resident all year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an Arizona resident for the whole year?
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, married filing separately, head of household or married filing jointly
      `my federal adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `my Arizona additions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your additions to income under A.R.S. s 43-1021 (for example, interest on other states' bonds), in US dollars
      `blind people` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (and your spouse on a joint return) are blind?
      `people 65 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of you (and your spouse on a joint return) were 65 or older and are not someone else's dependent?
      `older people whose care I pay for` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many people 65 or older did you pay for care as A.R.S. s 43-1023(B) describes?
      `stillbirths` IS A NUMBER @desc How many stillbirths with a certificate occurred in your household this year?
      `parents at home I support` IS A NUMBER @desc How many parents or grandparents 65 or older needing daily help lived with you all year, mostly supported by you?
      `my public pension` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal, Arizona state or Arizona local government pension you received, in US dollars
      `my taxable Social Security` IS A NUMBER @desc The Social Security or Railroad Retirement benefits included in your federal adjusted gross income, in US dollars
      `my military retired pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Uniformed services retired or retainer pay you received, in US dollars
      `my other subtractions` IS A NUMBER @desc Any other subtractions under A.R.S. s 43-1022, in US dollars
      `I take the standard deduction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you take the standard deduction rather than itemise?
      `my itemized deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your itemized deductions, if you itemise, in US dollars
      `my charitable gifts` IS A NUMBER @desc Charitable contributions you made, in US dollars
      `the standard deduction the department set` IS A NUMBER @desc The Department of Revenue's inflation-adjusted standard deduction for your status and year (0 to use the statute's 2025 figure)
      `year of the revenue notice for the flat rate` IS A NUMBER @desc The year the Department of Revenue received the A.R.S. s 43-243(B)(2) revenue notice that brings in the 2.5% flat rate (0 if not received)
      `dependents under 17` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents were under 17 at the end of the year?
      `dependents 17 or older` IS A NUMBER @desc How many dependents were 17 or older at the end of the year?
      `someone claims me as a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does another taxpayer claim you as a dependent?
      `I was in custody 60 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you sentenced to at least 60 days of the year in prison or jail?
      `residents in my household` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Arizona residents in your household (you, your spouse, your dependents) have an exemption on your return?
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`How much Arizona income tax do I owe` MEANS
    `the tax after credits` (`Return` WITH
        `tax year`                                          IS `tax year`
        `full-year resident`                                IS `I was a resident all year`
        `status`                                            IS `my filing status`
        `federal adjusted gross income`                     IS `my federal adjusted gross income`
        `additions`                                         IS `my Arizona additions`
        `exemption facts`                                   IS (`Exemption facts` WITH
            `blind persons qualifying`                          IS `blind people`
            `persons 65 or older qualifying`                    IS `people 65 or older`
            `persons 65 or older whose care I pay for`          IS `older people whose care I pay for`
            `stillbirths in the year`                           IS `stillbirths`
            `parents 65 or older living with me whom I support` IS `parents at home I support`)
        `public pensions received`                          IS `my public pension`
        `Social Security included in federal AGI`           IS `my taxable Social Security`
        `uniformed services retired pay`                    IS `my military retired pay`
        `other subtractions`                                IS `my other subtractions`
        `elects the standard deduction`                     IS `I take the standard deduction`
        `itemized deductions`                               IS `my itemized deductions`
        `charitable contributions`                          IS `my charitable gifts`
        `the department's standard deduction for the year`  IS `the standard deduction the department set`
        `year of the s 43-243(B)(2) notice`                 IS `year of the revenue notice for the flat rate`
        -- not read by any rule: paragraph 8 is not computed (placeholder)
        `year of the s 43-243(A) or (B)(1) notice`          IS 0
        `dependents under 17`                               IS `dependents under 17`
        `dependents 17 or older`                            IS `dependents 17 or older`
        `claimed as a dependent by another taxpayer`        IS `someone claims me as a dependent`
        `sentenced to custody for 60 days or more`          IS `I was in custody 60 days`
        `residents in the household for the excise credit`  IS `residents in my household`)
